# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so it must repeat
# everything .gitignore excludes — otherwise node_modules and friends get
# uploaded. Keep the two in sync.
#
# Why it exists: an EAS build failed with
#   EBUSY: resource busy or locked, copyfile 'android/.gradle/8.14.3/checksums/checksums.lock'
# because a local `gradlew assembleRelease` was running and holding that lock
# while EAS tried to copy the project. Native build state is worthless to a
# remote build — this project is CNG, so EAS runs `expo prebuild` itself and
# regenerates android/ and ios/ from app.json.

# --- mirrored from .gitignore ---
node_modules/
.tamagui/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
/ios
/android
.anonkey

# --- belt and braces: never upload native build state ---
# /android and /ios above already cover these, but they are spelled out so that
# re-adding the native folders to source control later cannot silently start
# uploading gigabytes of lock files and caches again.
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.cxx/
ios/build/
ios/Pods/
**/*.lock
!package-lock.json
!yarn.lock

# Local-only material that must never reach a build server.
.env
supabase/functions/.env
supabase/.temp/
scripts/__pycache__/
